<% content_for :page_title, "About the Canadiana Collection - #{application_name}" %>

<div class="home-page">
  <section class="site-section about-intro about-intro--canadiana">
    <div class="canadiana-shell about-intro-grid about-intro-grid--canadiana">
      <div class="about-intro-copy about-intro-copy--canadiana">
        <h1 class="section-title">About the Canadiana Collection</h1>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Approximately 31.5 million pages of publications that show how knowledge, stories, and information were shared over time.
          This collection includes books, newspapers, magazines, government documents, maps, and more from c. 1500 to the present day.
          Canadiana content is largely drawn from the Canadian Institute for Historic Micro-reproductions (CIHM) microfiche series.
        </p>
      </div>
      <%= render partial: 'shared/canadiana_stack', locals: { count: 12, collection: :canadiana } %>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="site-section about-modern-section about-modern-section--canadiana">
  <div class="canadiana-shell about-modern-layout">
    <section class="about-modern-feature-grid" aria-labelledby="canadiana-overview-title">
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--copy about-modern-card--canadiana-copy-primary">
        <h2>31.5 million pages in one collection</h2>
        <p>
          Browse materials spanning approximately five centuries of Canadian publishing, from early imprints to twentieth-century
          periodicals and documents.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--media about-modern-card--canadiana-image-primary">
        <a href="https://www.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.8_06349_193304/1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <img src="<%= asset_path('about/canadiana/oocihm.8_06349_193304.1.jpg') %>" alt="Historic books and publications from the Canadiana Collection" loading="lazy">
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--media about-modern-card--canadiana-image-secondary">
        <a href="https://www.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.8_06967_385/1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <img src="<%= asset_path('about/canadiana/oocihm.8_06967_385.1.jpg') %>" alt="Historic map materials from the Canadiana Collection" loading="lazy">
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--copy about-modern-card--canadiana-copy-secondary">
        <h2>A trusted resource for nearly 50 years</h2>
        <p>
          The Canadiana Collections and Infrastructure has grown alongside generations of researchers, continually
          expanding, modernizing, and adapting to new ways of working with knowledge.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="about-modern-block about-modern-deep-dive" aria-labelledby="canadiana-deep-dive-title">
      <div class="about-modern-block-head">
        <h2 id="canadiana-deep-dive-title">What you can find in the Canadiana Collection</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-modern-detail-stack" data-about-detail-stack>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-stack__pin">
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-books" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-books-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-books-title">Books and Publications</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            This collection brings together books and pamphlets that document more than three centuries of Canadian print culture.
            It supports research across history, literature, politics, religion, science, and everyday life, while remaining
            approachable for students and general readers beginning work on Canada. Titles were selected and digitized from more
            than 200 libraries and archives, and the collection includes both well-known works and rarer items identified through
            later surveys of special collections and uncatalogued holdings.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Books and Publications summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">98,000 titles</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Coverage to 1920</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">47 languages</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> The core focus is Canadian imprints to 1920. Selected works published abroad by
            Canadian authors, or closely related to Canada, were also included under the guidance of scholars and collection specialists.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid about-modern-detail-grid--single">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>All Books and Publications microfilmed by the Canadian Institute for Historical Microreproductions (CIHM)</li>
              <li>All Books and Publications available on Early Canadiana Online (ECO)</li>
              <li>Recently digitized Books and Publications never before published by Canadiana</li>
              <li>Strong coverage in women's history, Indigenous history, immigration, law, politics, medicine, and Canadian literature</li>
              <li>Titles in 47 different languages, including in 14 Indigenous languages</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Monographs+%7C+Monographies&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Books and Publications</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-serials" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-serials-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-serials-title">Newspapers and Magazines</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            This collection preserves newspapers, magazines, and other serial publications that show how Canadians debated events,
            built communities, and represented everyday life. It is valuable for formal research, but also easy to use for readers
            exploring public opinion, popular culture, and local history.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Newspapers and Magazines summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">1,700 periodical titles, plus annuals and newspapers</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Annuals to 1900</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Periodicals to 1920</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Newspapers to 1930</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> The collection includes annuals to 1900, periodicals to 1920, and newspapers to 1930.
            Periodical selection drew heavily on the Early Canadian Periodicals project and the advice of an expert committee.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid about-modern-detail-grid--single">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>All annuals and periodicals microfilmed by the Canadian Institute for Historical Microreproductions (CIHM)</li>
              <li>All periodicals available on Early Canadiana Online (ECO)</li>
              <li>Newspapers and Magazines recently added to our collection and are not available on ECO or in the CIHM fiche collection</li>
              <li>Local, trade, religious, and student newspapers and journals</li>
              <li>City directories and annual reports from churches, schools, businesses and other organizations</li>
              <li>Specialized periodicals covering literature, science, education, agriculture, politics, religion, sport, and more</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Serials+%7C+Publications+en+se%CC%81rie&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Newspapers and Magazines</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-government" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-government-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-government-title">Government Publications</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            This collection gathers official publications that show how governments in and around Canada recorded decisions,
            administered policy, and defined public life before 1900. It gives researchers and students direct access to the
            documentary record of law, governance, and administration.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Government Publications summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">8,500 books and publications; 79 series titles</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Pre-1900 focus</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Colonial and federal records</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> The collection grew out of the Early Official Publications project. It emphasizes
            pre-1900 colonial and federal material; municipal publications and later provincial publications are generally excluded.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid about-modern-detail-grid--single">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>A selection of pre-Confederation official government publications produced by colonial legislatures, such as acts, legislative debates, legislative journals, and sessional papers</li>
              <li>A selection of federal government documents published 1867-1900, such as acts, parliamentary debates, parliamentary journals, royal commission reports and sessional papers</li>
              <li>Pre-1900 publications from France and Great Britain that relate to the governance of Canada</li>
              <li>Civil service lists, 1885-1900</li>
              <li>Official guides for prospective immigrants to Canada and selected speeches by major political figures</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Government+Publications+%7C+Publications+gouvernementales&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Government Publications</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-maps" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-maps-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-maps-title">Maps</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            The Maps collection offers nearly 22,000 digitized Canadian maps from the 1:50,000 scale National Topographic Series.
            It supports spatial and environmental research, while also helping non-specialists visualize how places, boundaries,
            and infrastructure changed over time. The maps were digitized by McGill University Library and shared through a
            partnership with CRKN, marking the first major addition of member-contributed content to the Canadiana collection.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Maps summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">Approximately 22,000 maps</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">1905 to 2012</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">National Topographic Series 1:50,000</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> The present focus is the 1:50,000 scale National Topographic Series. The set is not yet complete,
            and additional sheets or other map series may be added as they become available.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid about-modern-detail-grid--single">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>Approximately 22,000 digitized maps from the National Topographic Series at 1:50,000 scale</li>
              <li>Coverage from 1905 to 2012 across all Canadian provinces and territories</li>
              <li>Useful for spatial history, environmental research, and the study of changing boundaries and infrastructure</li>
              <li>Parts of the series are also available through Scholars GeoPortal and Borealis, where georeferenced versions support open geospatial research and historical analysis</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Maps+%7C+Cartes&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Maps</a>
        </div>
      </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-modern-block about-modern-block--use" aria-labelledby="canadiana-use-title">
      <div class="about-modern-work-grid">
        <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--steps">
          <h2 id="canadiana-use-title">How to Work with the Collection</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Start broad:</strong> Use Basic Search to identify promising records, then narrow with filters for monographs, serials, maps, or government publications.</li>
            <li><strong>Refine queries:</strong> Apply methods from <a href="<%= navigating_collections_path(lang: I18n.locale) %>">Navigating the Collections</a>, including exact phrases in quotes and operators like <code>?</code>, <code>*</code>, <code>-</code>, and <code>|</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Save evidence:</strong> When relevant records appear, capture <code>IMG</code>, <code>PAGE</code>, and <code>FULL</code> (if available), then copy the persistent URL.</li>
            <li><strong>Cite correctly:</strong> Follow the <a href="<%= citation_guide_path(lang: I18n.locale) %>">Citation Guide</a>, cite Canadiana as the source, and include the persistent URL.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
        <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--media">
          <a href="https://www.canadiana.ca/view/oocihm.9_01973_3_1/2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img src="<%= asset_path('about/canadiana/oocihm.9_01973_3_1.2.jpg') %>" alt="Research workflow for Canadiana materials" loading="lazy">
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-modern-block about-modern-block--faq" aria-labelledby="canadiana-faq-title">
      <div class="about-modern-block-head">
        <h2 id="canadiana-faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-modern-faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>What time period does the Canadiana Collection cover?</summary>
          <p>The collection includes materials from roughly 1500 to the present day, with especially strong coverage of pre-Confederation and early modern publication history.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How were materials selected for digitization?</summary>
          <p>Selection was guided by collection specialists and scholars, with emphasis on Canadian imprints, high-use historical sources, and materials that support broad interdisciplinary study.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I search inside documents?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Full-text and metadata search are available where text extraction exists, alongside title, creator, and subject searching.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is this collection suitable for teaching as well as research?</summary>
          <p>Yes. The range of formats and topics supports undergraduate instruction, graduate seminars, and advanced scholarly projects.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
